1
00:00:02,187 --> 00:00:05,860
Hi everyone, today I'll talk
about the "side ride".

2
00:00:05,926 --> 00:00:14,858
[Music]

3
00:00:14,924 --> 00:00:19,218
The "side ride" is the kind of trick
you can't do holding on to anything,

4
00:00:19,284 --> 00:00:23,831
and it's hard for someone to hold you,
so you just have to go for it.

5
00:00:23,897 --> 00:00:29,937
Set the pedal fairly high

6
00:00:30,003 --> 00:00:34,458
and a bit forward,
which makes the first push easier.

7
00:00:34,524 --> 00:00:39,838
So set the pedal like this,
put your other foot on it,

8
00:00:39,904 --> 00:00:41,823
and then give it a try.

9
00:00:41,889 --> 00:00:51,155
[Music]

10
00:00:51,221 --> 00:00:54,828
For the "side ride",
there are two hand positions:

11
00:00:54,894 --> 00:00:58,336
you can hold one hand on each side
of the saddle,

12
00:00:58,402 --> 00:01:03,443
or put one in the middle
and hold the other one in front.

13
00:01:04,107 --> 00:01:08,607
As for weight in this trick,
shift most of your weight onto the saddle

14
00:01:08,673 --> 00:01:12,548
and keep as little weight as possible
on the foot on the pedal.

15
00:01:13,154 --> 00:01:17,073
It's also important to tell yourself
that with every pedal stroke,

16
00:01:17,139 --> 00:01:19,060
when the pedal comes up,

17
00:01:19,126 --> 00:01:22,134
you try to keep your foot
as light as you can,

18
00:01:22,200 --> 00:01:24,968
and put as much weight
as you can on the saddle.

19
00:01:25,594 --> 00:01:29,435
Don't try to keep the unicycle
straight, perpendicular to the ground,

20
00:01:29,501 --> 00:01:31,068
because it won't work like that.

21
00:01:31,134 --> 00:01:36,740
Tilt the unicycle slightly
so your weight stays above the axle.

22
00:01:36,806 --> 00:01:43,368
[Music]

23
00:01:43,434 --> 00:01:45,664
Something else I find important

24
00:01:45,730 --> 00:01:51,048
when you start the "side ride"
is to remember to keep your body above,

25
00:01:51,114 --> 00:01:53,855
that is, above the axle
and above the saddle.

26
00:01:53,921 --> 00:01:57,067
And keep in mind that this trick turns.

27
00:01:57,133 --> 00:02:00,921
Since the unicycle is tilted,
you automatically ride in circles.

28
00:02:00,987 --> 00:02:05,080
So during the "side ride", you lean
a bit like this and aim your body

29
00:02:05,146 --> 00:02:07,427
along a sort of diagonal.

30
00:02:10,074 --> 00:02:13,527
As for the starting position,
I think the easiest way is to start

31
00:02:13,607 --> 00:02:19,160
with the unicycle at your side,
put one foot on the pedal and go for it.

32
00:02:22,834 --> 00:02:25,434
You can also start from a "crank idle",

33
00:02:25,500 --> 00:02:31,234
or by putting one foot on the tire

34
00:02:31,300 --> 00:02:35,420
and then bringing the other one
onto the pedal.

35
00:02:40,667 --> 00:02:42,901
Alright, I'll finish with a few tips.

36
00:02:42,967 --> 00:02:48,754
It's important not to lean back,
because if you do, you'll never make it,

37
00:02:48,820 --> 00:02:53,967
since your weight won't be placed right
to do several wheel turns.

38
00:02:54,534 --> 00:02:56,641
Also, don't get discouraged,

39
00:02:56,707 --> 00:02:58,880
because you'll often manage
a first wheel turn,

40
00:02:58,946 --> 00:03:02,115
but then it takes time
to get more than one.

41
00:03:02,181 --> 00:03:04,881
I'd say you've got this trick down

42
00:03:04,947 --> 00:03:07,394
once you can do two or three wheel turns.

43
00:03:07,460 --> 00:03:12,994
Before that, it's easy,
but you haven't mastered the position yet.

44
00:03:13,060 --> 00:03:19,123
And finally, what helped me was getting
into the "pissing dog" position.

45
00:03:19,189 --> 00:03:22,180
The other leg, the one not on the wheel,
should be lifted a bit

46
00:03:22,204 --> 00:03:24,268
into this "pissing dog" position.

47
00:03:24,801 --> 00:03:28,800
And that helps you get the right position
and the right movement.

48
00:03:30,621 --> 00:03:34,187
Lastly, I'll show you a few transitions

49
00:03:34,253 --> 00:03:39,347
with the "side ride",
but this trick has loads of transitions.

50
00:03:40,061 --> 00:03:42,077
Alright, now it's your turn.

51
00:03:42,143 --> 00:03:44,800
Have a great session and good luck!

52
00:03:44,866 --> 00:04:11,779
[Music]

